@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+---
+id: task-005-implement-rfc-6902-json-patch-createpatch-diff
+type: task
+title: "Implement RFC 6902 JSON Patch createPatch (diff)"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two versions of a JSON document, instead of the whole
+new version. Export `createPatch(from, to)` from `src/index.ts`: it returns a JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+that turns `from` into `to` when applied, without mutating either input, describing only what changed
+and nothing more (no whole-document replace for a small, localised difference).
+
+## What was done
+
+- Extended `src/index.test.ts` first (red): confirmed the suite failed to import the missing
+  `createPatch` export, then wrote the full set of tests before touching `src/index.ts` — an empty
+  patch for equal documents, no-mutation of both inputs, single `add`/`remove`/`replace` for a lone
+  changed/added/removed member, recursion into nested objects, reference-token escaping (`~`, `/`) in
+  generated paths, array element `replace` at an unchanged index, trailing array `add`/`remove` for
+  length changes, a whole-document `replace` at `""` when `from`/`to` differ in kind at the root, a
+  round-trip through `applyPatch` on a larger mixed document, a `"__proto__"`-named member round-trip
+  (style matching the existing `applyPatch`/`applyMergePatch` tests), and a check that an added value
+  is cloned rather than aliased with `to`.
+- Implemented `createPatch` in `src/index.ts` (green):
+  - `diffValues(from, to, path, patch)` is the shared recursive step: returns immediately (no
+    operation) when `from` and `to` are already deeply equal (reusing the existing `deepEqual`), then
+    dispatches to `diffObjects` when both sides are JSON objects, to `diffArrays` when both are arrays,
+    and otherwise appends one `replace` at `path` with a clone of `to` — this last branch is what
+    produces the single whole-document `replace` when `createPatch` is called on two values that
+    differ in kind at the root, since the initial call is `diffValues(from, to, '', patch)`.
+  - `diffObjects` walks `from`'s keys, emitting `remove` for a key `to` no longer has and recursing via
+    `diffValues` for a key both share, then walks `to`'s keys for ones `from` never had, emitting `add`
+    with a clone of the new value. Each path segment is built with a new `escapeToken` helper (the
+    inverse of the existing `unescapeToken`), so member names containing `~` or `/` round-trip through
+    the generated pointer correctly.
+  - `diffArrays` recurses with `diffValues` over the shared index range (so a changed element at a
+    fixed index gets its own minimal nested diff instead of a wholesale element replace), then appends
+    trailing `remove`s (from the highest leftover index down, so an earlier removal in the list can't
+    shift the index a later one still needs) or trailing `add`s at `"-"` for any leftover length
+    difference. Recorded as dl-004: this is a positional diff, not an LCS alignment, so a middle
+    insertion/deletion in a large array is not detected as such.
+  - `createPatch(from, to)` is just `diffValues(from, to, '', patch)` over a fresh `patch` array.
+    Every value placed into an operation goes through the existing `clone`, so no part of the result
+    is aliased with `from` or `to`; neither input is ever written to.
+- Verified with `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build` and `npm test`: 89/89 tests passing (18 new), and
+  `node --test --experimental-test-coverage` reports 100% line/branch/function coverage on
+  `src/index.ts`, no regression from the existing baseline.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- dl-004 records the choice of a positional (non-LCS) array diff and its trade-off; submitted
+  alongside this task for approval.
